## Bug Count Config Changes
Previous parsing of config in the notebook:
https://github.com/sailuh/kaiaulu/blob/5bbdbb2834df02971e604cb20207f2d25e3acc56/vignettes/bug_count.Rmd#L39-L52

Before it would parse through one config file, I will be splitting the configuration between immutable vs mutable data. The notebook will then be able to parse through split configuration (project + analysis).

## Task List

- [x] See if notebook can run with geronimo_immutable.yml + analysisE.yml.
- [x] Reconfigure bug_count.Rmd to take the split configs

Further expanding on issue #359 , focusing on the coding specification to create a notebook that takes all yml files in config and treat them like data. Based on 2 user cases:

A) Researcher who needs to analyze a lot of projects/data (many projects, few analyses)
B) Project Manager who has to monitor just a small set of projects (few projects, many analyses)

This new notebook will be able to take all configs in the folder, both immutable and mutable, and generate summaries of relating data. Will be further discussing what this entails.

### My current vision:
Reasoning behind wanting to analyze all configs is to see the comparisons between the files. For example, generating a table that shows which configs use certain filters or which ones are missing certain fields (e.g. tools, depends).

### Ideas I have:

- Generates a table (possibly project x sections yml file used)
- Statistic table (e.g. how many projects use gitlog?)

# Refactoring Notebooks
## Purpose
Splitting Configuration files for depends and understand notebooks, similar to issue #359 .

Currently, configuration files are mixed with both config data types, immutable and mutable data. Will be making it so that the notebooks will take two configurations when running analyses, one for project and another for analysis. 

## Scitools/Depends
Will be working with the two notebooks depends_showcase.Rmd and understand_showcase.Rmd. Associated notebook runs with helix.yml config file so that configuration will be split between immutable and analysis specific data.

### Table
Table that shows more closely which part of the configurations are used in the notebooks are shown in this comment, https://github.com/sailuh/kaiaulu/issues/366#issuecomment-4098078420.

## Line Metrics
Will be working with the one notebook line_metrics_showcase.Rmd. Associated notebook runs with apr.yml config file. I will be splitting the apr.yml config file into a immutable project yml (apr_immutable.yml) and mutable yml file (e.g. analysis1.yml).

### Table
Table shows which notebook is using which yml files + old configuration + new split sections of configurations. I also included a color coded version as well.

